.TH CVECTOR_AT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_at \- access an element at a specific index
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

void *cvector_at(cvec v, size_t index);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function gives a pointer to the element at the index that the caller
gives. The caller can use the pointer to read the element. The caller can
also use it to change the element in place.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v      Vector to access
index  Zero-based index of the element to access
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Gives a pointer to the element at the index on success
Gives NULL when index >= elem_count, and when the vector is empty
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(1) complexity
The pointer stays valid only until the size of the vector changes
The function asserts when v is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_at (3),
.BR cvector_elem_count (3)
